# Realms of Power: Magic — Overview (Lore)

**Version:** 0.4
**Source:** Ars Magica Fifth Edition — Realms of Power: Magic (Atlas Games)
**Publisher:** Atlas Games
**Edition:** arm5e (EXTENSION on the core rulebook)

> This file is a factual orientation to the supplement and an index into the
> Phase-2 corpus. It reproduces no invented lore. The book's narrative and
> Game-Master prose (chapter introductions, worked examples, story seeds and
> the 114 sidebars) is **not yet reproduced verbatim** — that pass is deferred
> for owner disposition (see DECISIONS-FOR-MORNING.md, RoP:Magic). The
> mechanical, enumerable content of the book IS converted, in the `.ttrpg`
> files listed below.

---

### What this book is

*Realms of Power: Magic* details the Magic Realm of Mythic Europe: its auras,
its inhabitants (magic animals, humans, spirits and things), and the mechanical
vocabulary — Magic Qualities and Inferiorities, new Virtues and Flaws, new
Abilities, and Common Magic Powers — used to build them. It is a supplement to
the Ars Magica Fifth Edition core rulebook and is loaded alongside it.

### The chapters (from the printed Contents)

- **I. Introduction** (p.5) — framing prose. No enumerable mechanics.
- **II. Magic Auras** (p.7) — how Magic auras work, tethers, and aura tables.
  Rules tables and sidebars here are **not yet converted** (owner disposition).
- **III. The Magic Realm** (p.17) — the nature of the realm and its powers.
  The **Common Magic Powers** insert (pp.38-39) is converted:
  `arm5e-rop-magic-0.5-common-magic-powers.ttrpg` (16). The **Magic Qualities
  and Inferiorities** (pp.36-37) are converted:
  `arm5e-rop-magic-0.5-magic-qualities.ttrpg` (49).
- **IV. Magic Characters** (p.29) — building magic beings. The **New & Modified
  Virtues and Flaws** are converted (`...-virtues-flaws.ttrpg`, 58 including 5
  MODIFY of core entries and one insert-only stub); the **New & Modified
  Abilities** are converted (`...-magic-abilities.ttrpg`, 3). Character-guide
  stat blocks appear in `...-statblocks.ttrpg`.
- **V. Magic Animals** (p.55), **VI. Magic Humans** (p.83), **VII. Magic
  Spirits** (p.100) — the magic-being types and their example stat blocks and
  type summaries are converted as soft, verbatim stat blocks in
  `...-statblocks.ttrpg` (74 total: 48 characters, 16 templates, 10 type
  summaries). Chapter narrative prose is not yet reproduced.
- **VIII. Magic Things** (p.119) — vis, Enrichment, and the **Things of
  Virtue** (herbs, objects, formed stones, trees). Converted as
  `...-things-of-virtue.ttrpg` (25), each carrying its verbatim Shape & Material
  bonus where the book prints one (13). The individual write-up prose is not
  reproduced — those write-ups are displaced in the source extraction (verified
  on Centaury and Oak), so no misattributed rules text is emitted; each entry
  points to its page.
- **Appendix: Book of Mundane Beasts** (p.140) — 12 mundane animal stat blocks,
  converted as `...-mundane-beasts.ttrpg` (soft, verbatim stats).

